--- TRANSCRIPT ---
{
  "tool": "search",
  "arguments": {
    "query": "impact of $100 micro‑grant farmed animal welfare reform effective altruism"
  }
}
{
  "result": [
    "Effective Altruism Forum post (2023) discusses that a $100 micro‑grant to farmed‑animal welfare reform typically funds a small advocacy campaign, reaching roughly 100,000 farm animals and improving their welfare marginally, but the cost‑effectiveness is low compared to other interventions.",
    "GiveWell analysis (2022) notes that farmed‑animal welfare reforms have high uncertainty and limited data on how a $100 grant translates to animal lives saved."
  ]
}
{
  "tool": "search",
  "arguments": {
    "query": "effectiveness of $100 micro‑grant insecticide‑treated bednets lives saved"
  }
}
{
  "result": [
    "GiveWell (2024) estimates that a $100 micro‑grant for insecticide‑treated bednets can fund distribution of about 5–7 bednets in high‑malaria regions, preventing an estimated 0.02–0.04 malaria deaths per dollar, translating to roughly 0.5–1 life saved per $100 grant.",
    "The Against Malaria Foundation reports that each $2.50 spent on a bednet saves an average of 0.0004 lives, making $100 sufficient for ~40 bednets and about 0.016 lives saved, a higher impact than many other health interventions."
  ]
}
